NAME
    userdel - remove a shell account

SYNOPSIS
    userdel <name>

DESCRIPTION
    Removes <name> from the process-wide account directory. Only 'root'
    may remove accounts. userdel refuses to remove 'root' itself or any
    account currently active in any live session (switch that session
    away with su(1) first).

EXAMPLES
    userdel guest

EXIT STATUS
    0   Account removed.
    1   Missing name, caller is not root, account does not exist,
        target is root, or account is currently in use.

SEE ALSO
    useradd(1), su(1), who(1), whoami(1)
